     zzmmaaiill is the mail client of the COHERENT GUI.  It must be
     run under the zzvviieeww desktop.  It reads the user's mailbox
     /uussrr/ssppooooll/mmaaiill/_n_a_m_e (the format used by 77mmaaiill) and shows a
     list of message headers - number, a DD mark, sender, date and
     subject - above a pane with the text of the selected mes-
     sage.  The newest message is selected at start-up, and the
     mailbox is polled for new mail every 15 seconds.  zzmmaaiill
     takes no file arguments; it accepts the standard window _o_p-
     _t_i_o_n_s of GUI applications; see zzvviieeww.

     The button bar offers NNeeww, RReeppllyy, DDeelleettee and PPuurrggee while
     reading, and SSeenndd and CCaanncceell while composing.  Keyboard com-
     mands while reading:

                ^PP, ^NN          select the previous / next message
                ^ZZ, ^BB          page the message text up
                ^VV, ^FF, SSPPAACCEE   page the message text down
                dd               toggle the delete mark on the message
                nn               compose a new message
                rr               reply to the selected message

     DDeelleettee only marks a message; nothing is removed from the
     mailbox until PPuurrggee, which asks for confirmation and
     rewrites the mailbox without the marked messages.

     Composing replaces the text pane with a TToo: field, a SSuubb-
     jjeecctt: field and a message body.  TAB and RETURN move from
     field to field into the body; ^P from the top of the body
